{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: reordered the model block so that each parameter prior (`a`, `b`, and `sigma`) appears before the likelihood statement that uses those parameters. This preserves the same Stan log density because sampling statements are additive. `N` and `x` remain unprotected context inputs.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int N;
  vector[N] x;
  vector[N] y;
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0> a;
  real<lower=0> b;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
}
model {
  a ~ normal(0, 10);
  b ~ normal(0, 10);
  sigma ~ normal(0, 10);
  y ~ normal(a * exp(-b * x), sigma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N": 5, "x": [4.4464461147199685, 6.652219031180259, 4.511262320723018, 2.549706929544839, 4.28385153389249], "y": [3.0, 3.0, 5.0, 5.0, 4.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
